4.  Implement `FromPov` which re-orients the tree so that the specified node 
becomes the new root. This involves finding the path from the original root to 
the target node, and then reversing the parent-child relationships along that 
path.

5.  Implement `PathTo` which finds the shortest path between two nodes. This can
be done by finding the path from the root to `from`, the path from the root to 
`to`, finding their lowest common ancestor (LCA), and combining the paths.



